---
description: Prompt for GitHub pushes only when meaningful project changes have accumulated
alwaysApply: true
---

# Milestone Git Pushes

- Do not prompt to push after small, isolated, cosmetic, or work-in-progress changes.
- Let related changes accumulate into a coherent, verified milestone.
- Treat new features, architectural changes, database migrations, ML model updates, security fixes, deployment changes, and substantial documentation baselines as major changes.
- After a major change is complete and relevant checks pass, ask the user whether they want it committed and pushed to GitHub.
- Summarize what would be included before asking.
- Never push automatically unless the user explicitly authorizes that push.
